# Arabic / RTL

The website is Arabic-first and RTL.

## HTML

The application should use:

dir="rtl"

and:

lang="ar"

where appropriate.

## CSS

Prefer logical CSS properties.

Use:

margin-inline
padding-inline
inset-inline
border-start-start-radius
border-start-end-radius

Avoid unnecessary:

margin-left
margin-right
padding-left
padding-right

unless direction-specific behavior is explicitly required.

## Icons

Icons must respect RTL direction.

Directional icons such as:
- arrows
- chevrons
- navigation icons

should visually communicate the correct direction.

Do not blindly mirror every icon.

Icons such as:
- search
- phone
- mail
- settings

normally do not need mirroring.

## Typography

Arabic typography must be readable and professional.

Choose an Arabic font deliberately.

Avoid mixing many fonts.

Maintain consistent:
- font weights
- line heights
- heading sizes

## Text

Do not alter official company content casually.

Preserve the meaning of the source material.

Correct obvious OCR errors when converting the PDF content into website content, but do not invent new claims.

## Layout

Ensure:

- text alignment is correct
- navigation works correctly
- cards work correctly in RTL
- grids do not visually break
- icons do not point in the wrong direction

## Accessibility

Arabic screen-reader content must remain meaningful.

Do not replace text with icons alone.